ReadMe

Class Name: SpecimenTrackingApp

Difficulty: Level 3 — Object-Oriented Problem Solving

Estimated Time: 70–90 minutes

Actual Time Taken: 78 minutes

Written by: Chanwoo Park

Problem
Create a laboratory specimen chain-of-custody tracker.
Specimens must move through a controlled workflow and laboratory stations
must enforce their workload capacity.

Program Flow
- Create a SpecimenRegistry.
- Register laboratory stations.
- Register several specimens.
- Assign specimens to stations.
- Start and complete analysis.
- Archive completed specimens.
- Trigger several invalid operations and handle their exceptions.
- Print a final specimen-status report.

Class Responsibilities
- SpecimenTrackingApp: Runs the scenario, catches business exceptions, and prints output.
- Specimen: Owns specimen data and protects its workflow state.
- LabStation: Owns station capacity and active assigned specimens.
- SpecimenRegistry: Stores/searches objects and coordinates their collaboration.
- SpecimenStatus: Defines valid specimen workflow states.
- InvalidSpecimenOperationException: Represents invalid workflow operations.

Requirements
- Use List reference types for registry collections.
- Protect specimen status from arbitrary external modification.
- Keep station capacity and specimen assignment consistent.
- Propagate business-operation exceptions to this console class.
- Demonstrate valid and invalid workflow cases.
- Print a final status summary.

Learning Objective
Practice object ownership, encapsulation, controlled state transitions,
collection abstraction, exception propagation, and responsibility separation.